  "headline": "MPR Verification Team Confirms Eligibility Of Vice President Candidates",
  "seoTitle": "MPR Verification Team Confirms Vice President Candidates",
  "metaDescription": "The MPR verification team confirmed the eligibility of Andi Amran Sulaiman and Sugiono, granting candidates four days to complete any outstanding…",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The MPR verification team confirmed that the population documents for vice presidential candidates Andi Amran Sulaiman and Sugiono meet all requirements.",
    "Verification officials validated a name change for Andi Amran Sulaiman based on a 2022 court ruling following discrepancies in his high school diploma.",
    "Candidates are permitted a four-day window to rectify or complete any outstanding administrative requirements before the final selection process."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) of Indonesia is currently overseeing the verification process for vice presidential candidates following the vacancy left by Gibran. A dedicated verification team has been conducting factual checks on candidates Andi Amran Sulaiman and Sugiono, including visits to the Supreme Court, the Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK), the National Police, and the Ministry of Finance. During this process, the team confirmed that population documents for both candidates align with regulatory requirements. Specifically, officials addressed a naming discrepancy in Andi Amran Sulaiman's high school diploma, confirming it as legitimate based on a 2022 court decision. The MPR has scheduled the plenary session for the vice presidential election for December 10 and 11, 2026. Candidates currently have a four-day period to finalize any outstanding administrative requirements as the MPR continues to monitor health evaluations and legal documentation.",
